{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Prime-by-Prime_Optimization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Prime-by-Prime Optimization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Solution_1_but_Fewer_Notations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Solution 1 but Fewer Notations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Guesswork)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Guesswork)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Simple_Explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Simple Explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Calculus_Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Calculus Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05725a6508fe8df761c6e91d2735b697ebd87d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> denote the number of positive integers that divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41be0747bbf7001b9329b476eed5b4b71bd06f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(1)=1,d(2)=2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507662884dca473ae601a786566e5bc9f111260d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(12)=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. (This function is known as the divisor function.) Let<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e0a31875f03c4b386a006e694adbb03555a964.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)=\\frac{d(n)}{\\sqrt [3]n}.\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" />There is a unique positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/4514eacf727d73adee1972fc2a7afa6da93edc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(N)&gt;f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d3171a0f7ce2bd1a192890f0c3a49f81f84fffbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ne N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cf31acc4d19289fd14d58e39c17cff9fe2b0e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N?$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb8df52cefa7ae591ab34f7f53adbf0ce95882e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }5 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }6 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }7 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }8\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Prime-by-Prime_Optimization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Prime-by-Prime_Optimization)\">Solution 1 (Prime-by-Prime Optimization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Prime-by-Prime Optimization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We consider the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d5dbb87dfb42bdebf7025f8c5eb7243c949aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n:$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43ff4c18c34b1de40663c0d0208a0b11cfc629e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}p_i^{e_i}.\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"50\" /> By the Multiplication Principle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651a7c36a4c518e2a28fb386b03abefaffe077a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d(n)=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}(e_i+1).\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"50\" /> Now, we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327fe537324aa45bc7cee44ace1d7a7dfb389caa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)=\\frac{d(n)}{\\sqrt [3]n}=\\frac{\\prod_{i=1}^{k}(e_i+1)}{\\prod_{i=1}^{k}p_i^{e_i/3}}=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\frac{e_i+1}{p_i^{{e_i}/3}}.\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"51\" /> As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9d07650d9bbc1412cbd51b2f268ad3961cf4ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe9a362a0af9933e24abf9d8d9c541ac0f15b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)&gt;f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/721b0c7a7d2811125891983671d266e6e0d7a19d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)^3&gt;f(b)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6583a799ce46b06b1cceb493abb45a07c88fd6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b.$\" width=\"11\" height=\"12\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is maximized if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18aafbaecb38dc73d8355c34a574bba092bf658.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)^3=\\prod_{i=1}^{k}\\frac{(e_i+1)^3}{p_i^{{e_i}}}\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"50\" /> is maximized.\n</p><p>We also allow <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8aa488d21fa6be0f1846ea9718bdf57005d6e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> corresponding to the prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> not appearing in the prime factorization.\n</p><p>For each prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c699725218958e044a4f271042b0b40b9ed713f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f848cca756b6aae95e1b66879b669042adbfa553.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_p(e)=\\frac{(e+1)^3}{p^e},\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" /> so maximizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cbaba089c658b9330d4fec947793e19c02b280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"21\" /> becomes choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e48834b16f5cc8d66aadb6ea8cb6de9f76fc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_p(e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> for each prime independently. For consecutive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1a14d1e9e927e52a967603fd2426328bc5e03c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425b19364d519105211272ce42722c02c1ffe2bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{g_p(e+1)}{g_p(e)}=\\frac{(e+2)^3/p^{e+1}}{(e+1)^3/p^e}=\\frac{1}{p}\\cdot\\frac{(e+2)^3}{(e+1)^3}.\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"44\" /> Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e92541f18a5ece0bea3f9e42d2d130d0cf1c413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{e+2}{e+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"46\" height=\"40\" /> strictly decreases, so does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b4c5fe796d9513b2d97c10f6ed0960597243ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{g_p(e+1)}{g_p(e)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"81\" height=\"45\" /> For each prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c699725218958e044a4f271042b0b40b9ed713f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e48834b16f5cc8d66aadb6ea8cb6de9f76fc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_p(e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> increases while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f821238e6c25cc27bf975b05facd4b9a4ce0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{g_p(e+1)}{g_p(e)}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"109\" height=\"45\" /> and, because these ratios strictly decrease, it decreases forever once the ratio drops below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Thus the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709ce3966c2ad40fe1d10ec3b4acdc362ba7044f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{g_p(e+1)}{g_p(e)}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"109\" height=\"45\" /> is the maximizing exponent.\n</p><p>We construct the following table:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67403c35b4c3f09923d258d54fc14b22988b642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c|c}  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2.25ex] \\boldsymbol{i} &amp; \\boldsymbol{p_i} &amp; \\boldsymbol{e_i} &amp; \\boldsymbol{\\dfrac{(e_i+1)^3}{p_i^{e_i}}} &amp; \\textbf{Max?} \\\\ [2.5ex] \\hline\\hline  &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; \\\\      &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; 4 &amp; \\\\     &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; 27/4 &amp;\\\\     &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; 8 &amp; \\checkmark\\\\     &amp; &amp; 4 &amp; 125/16 &amp; \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp;\\\\     &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; 8/3 &amp; \\\\     &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp;  \\checkmark\\\\     &amp; &amp; 3 &amp; 64/27 &amp;  \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] 3 &amp; 5 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp;  \\\\     &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; 8/5 &amp;  \\checkmark\\\\     &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; 27/25 &amp; \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] 4 &amp; 7 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp;  \\\\     &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; 8/7 &amp;  \\checkmark\\\\     &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; 27/49 &amp; \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline   &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\geq5 &amp; \\geq11 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; \\checkmark \\\\     &amp; &amp; \\geq1 &amp; \\leq8/11 &amp;   \\\\ [0.5ex] \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"446\" />\nFinally, the positive integer we seek is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e33cf001501422a8aea45f60f1e6d78a0dff97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^3\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1=2520.$\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" /> The sum of its digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7b313639299dd6b3e7cc78daa094ea9576d5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+5+2+0=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"185\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, once we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35672a19103f2ead1f02935bb8450addc3318b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> we can conclude that the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Only choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is possible.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Solution_1_but_Fewer_Notations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Solution_1_but_Fewer_Notations)\">Solution 2 (Solution 1 but Fewer Notations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Solution 1 but Fewer Notations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The question statement asks for the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> that maximizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a64e9e34427e2ecf68b622ee5cb131e0f1cce09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> start out at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; we will find what factors to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by, in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to maximize the function.\n</p><p>First, we will find what power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by. If we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456a366cf7ae50d0ea4705904567cf8f5fa5d045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a}$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />, the numerator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56fefdd4a9ed5861e00bf7b3e804e1923482c54d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, will multiply by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />; this is because the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456a366cf7ae50d0ea4705904567cf8f5fa5d045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a}$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> divisors. The denominator, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2caab46283dbe2363ab6ba0e3d2d1255bd5632e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, will simply multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/9826dc17fb82de1dfaf534ac2f31eb045eeaca28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{2^{a}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, the entire function multiplies by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eee6b57c1ffc7c17b94571f6eda8f1f3380c696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{\\sqrt[3]{2^{a}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"47\" height=\"43\" />. We want to find the integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that maximizes this value. By inspection, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; right now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we will find what power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by. Similar to the previous step, we wish to find the integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that maximizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da2b67135e673fe4f14a8d861d7d710cb4fd62b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{\\sqrt[3]{3^{a}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"47\" height=\"43\" />. This value, also by inspection, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can repeat this step on the rest of the primes to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf435fbfaffde085aa4add6a6fe549e1df24230.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = 2^{3} \\cdot 3^{2} \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />\nbut from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> on, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> will maximize the value of the function, so the prime is not a factor in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00abb241eb42d7033ec2934d858d5f872fc9ee56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2520$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e96880a2ee1951870033a1cdbeb0ad262f7ac19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fast)\">Solution 3 (Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the answer choices to our advantage, we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by 9 without explicitly computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, by exploiting the following fact:\n</p><p><b>Claim</b>: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by 3, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52abeb2b3ac28bbb329c929b9868844085757b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(9n) &gt; f(3n) &gt; f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof</b>: Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c8d663fee90ee9b29319592620ab8601b13b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(\\cdot)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplicative_function\" title=\"Multiplicative function\">multiplicative function</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/6781ccd56c0912965ff22c282602b68034e37733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(3n) = d(3)d(n) = 2d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/7121bcdff9864f7e14e368c1d3d3d18b25490ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(9n) = 3d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f17a7cb9339e45aa1adca60d955048275c804b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(3n) &amp;= \\frac{2d(n)}{\\sqrt[3]{3n}} \\approx 1.38 f(n)\\\\ f(9n) &amp;= \\frac{3d(n)}{\\sqrt[3]{9n}} \\approx 1.44 f(n) \\end{align*}\" width=\"207\" height=\"92\" />\nNote that the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413127398883b135c56e82956e105d240414fcc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"27\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f093987bbe6bdb9a6dcde305a1cf49e85643169e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"27\" height=\"42\" /> do not have to be explicitly computed; we only need the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bd647eafbcad3f811ace253138da249c8f87520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{9}} &gt; \\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" /> which is easy to show by hand.\n</p><p>The above claim automatically implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of 9: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> was not divisible by 9, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b0c365eb84f68549fc63830e24c55252f9a452b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(9N) &gt; f(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> which is a contradiction, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> was divisible by 3 and not 9, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60fd46bb47f7296f2ea4e201c8d531a3050fe5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3N) &gt; f(N) &gt; f\\left(\\frac{N}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"198\" height=\"43\" />, also a contradiction. Then the sum of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be a multiple of 9, so only choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8d358cf664238c8dfcbfed4023aee71915891b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> works.\n</p><p>-scrabbler94\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Guesswork.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Guesswork)\">Solution 4 (Guesswork)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Guesswork)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem mentions the sum of digits - recall that if a number is divisible by 9, then so is the sum of its digits. Guess that the answer must therefore be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8d358cf664238c8dfcbfed4023aee71915891b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> .\n</p><p>- youtube.com/indianmathguy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Simple_Explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Simple_Explanation)\">Solution 5 (Simple Explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Simple Explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The aim of this problem is to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e76b9df1b5d7ce44676b1218c70e312788ca162a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(N).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let's start with when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has one prime factor. If this is the case, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be its exponent. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be the prime factor because regardless of what prime we use, the numerator will only depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we must minimize the denominator. Therefore, in this case, we want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eee6b57c1ffc7c17b94571f6eda8f1f3380c696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{\\sqrt[3]{2^{a}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"47\" height=\"43\" /> (since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> factors). By inspection, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> does the job.\n</p><p>Now notice that we can add another prime factor to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since we can split up prime factors and multiplication under prime factorization and cube roots, we just need to maximize the same process for the second prime factor. Again, we go with the next least prime factor to minimize the denominator which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. To clarify, we want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2740384fabe21c0e4d0e487755a298e69e4bd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b+1}{\\sqrt[3]{3^{b}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"45\" height=\"44\" /> (letting the exponent be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />). Inspection again gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is maximal.\n</p><p>We repeat this process two more times, adding a prime factor for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We find by inspection that the maximizing power of 5 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the maximizing power of 7 is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Now, notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c107687c2fa648bc55e3ec49a0e770b408db9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then regardless of what exponent we put in the numerator, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86ab524e4519e3b7c5d7388df7400b949749ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\frac{d(n)}{\\sqrt [3]n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"100\" height=\"45\" /> will be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This is bad, because then our maximized value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a64e9e34427e2ecf68b622ee5cb131e0f1cce09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> will decrease. Noting that our next least prime factor is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we know that we are done.\n</p><p>We evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee8e36fc89ec250f77bb18fc831468939d90924e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^3*3^2*5^1*7^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"160\" height=\"17\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00abb241eb42d7033ec2934d858d5f872fc9ee56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2520$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e608c4f6c31100fc51b8839f7154d0f9b4c821c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+5+2+0 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"183\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~xHypotenuse\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Calculus_Remark\">Calculus Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Calculus Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the maximum of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e153531d35c29eee50e76b694e150c65d3ac8c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{a^{x/3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" /> for some prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by taking the derivative and setting it equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b6d778f9d3f5a5afc81638251db934a80d4220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = e^{-\\frac{x\\ln a}{3}}-\\frac{\\ln a}{3}xe^{-\\frac{x\\ln a}{3}}-\\frac{\\ln a}{3}e^{-\\frac{x\\ln a}{3}} = 0 \\to 1-\\frac{\\ln a}{3}x - \\frac{\\ln a}{3}=0 \\to \\frac{\\ln a}{3}x = 1-\\frac{\\ln a}{3} \\to x = \\frac{3}{\\ln a}\\left( 1-\\frac{\\ln a}{3} \\right) = \\frac{3}{\\ln a}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"990\" height=\"45\" />. This gives the exponents you need for each prime in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />; however, it outputs real numbers, not positive integers.\n</p><p>~ndv1tt\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gWaUNz0gLE0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gWaUNz0gLE0</a> (by Dedekind Cuts)\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6P-0ZHAaC_A\">https://youtu.be/6P-0ZHAaC_A</a> (by OmegaLearn) ~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">